ithub.com/repos/apache/airflow/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/deployments","created_at":"2015-04-13T18:04:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T14:39:15Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-29T14:43:56Z","git_url":"git://github.com/apache/airflow.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:apache/airflow.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow","homepage":"https://airflow.apache.org/","size":790917,"stargazers_count":47308,"watchers_count":47308,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":18214,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1927,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["airflow","apache","apache-airflow","automation","dag","data-engineering","data-integration","data-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/72474","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72474","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72474.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72474.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-28T10:07:47Z"},"body":"<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\r\n     https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 -->\r\n\r\n* **Project Board:** [AIP-85 Dag Importer (Project #672)](https://github.com/orgs/apache/projects/672)\r\n* **Related PR:** #72369 ([AIP-85] Move DAG importer abstractions and registry into Task SDK)\r\n\r\n### Why\r\n\r\nAIP-85 allows Dags to come from non-Python and composite sources (YAML/JSON importers,\r\n`ZipImporter`, external bundles). Three pieces of metadata currently assume a single local `.py` file:\r\n\r\n1. Import errors only track `filename`, but a Dag definition is no longer strictly 1:1 with a file —\r\n   an archive member inside a container (e.g. `archive.zip/dags/my_dag.py`) needs an abstract source\r\n   reference while retaining `filename` for compatibility.\r\n2. `DagWarning` rejects any type outside the built-in enum, preventing importers from reporting\r\n   format-specific warnings.\r\n3. Dag source is always highlighted as Python in the UI, regardless of the Dag's actual definition language.\r\n\r\nThis is groundwork for AIP-85: it introduces the necessary schema and model extensions without altering\r\nruntime behavior for existing Python Dags.\r\n\r\n### What\r\n\r\n**Import errors: add `source_reference`, keep `filename`**\r\n- Migration `ca8499dc1004` adds a nullable `source_reference` column (`String(2000)`) to `import_error`.\r\n- Retains `filename` as the primary file path column across the database, model, and API to preserve\r\n  full backward compatibility for existing tooling and API consumers.\r\n- Exposes `source_reference: str | None` on `ImportErrorResponse` and `ParseImportError`.\r\n- Implements `ParseImportError.full_file_path()` using `Path.is_absolute()` rather than substring prefix\r\n  matching, avoiding false positives across sibling bundle paths.\r\n- Streamlines `delete_dag` cleanup to delete import errors matching `source_reference` or `filename`.\r\n\r\n**Dag warnings: open-ended types, enum retained**\r\n- `DagWarning.__init__` accepts `DagWarningType | str`, normalizing enum members to their string value\r\n  and preserving importer-supplied warning types verbatim.\r\n- `DAGWarningResponse.warning_type` and the `list_dag_warnings` filter accept `DagWarningType | str`.\r\n  This retains `DagWarningType` in the published schema and generated clients as the vocabulary for\r\n  core-emitted warnings, while gracefully accepting importer-defined warnings.\r\n- Filtering by an unknown `warning_type` returns `200` with an empty list instead of `422`.\r\n\r\n**Dag source language**\r\n- Migration `e5a91c7f42b3` adds a nullable `language` column (`String(64)`) to `dag_code`.\r\n- `DAGSourceResponse` and `DagCode` persist and expose `language: str | None`.\r\n- UI Code view passes `code?.language ?? \"python\"` to Monaco `Editor` and `CodeDiffViewer`, defaulting\r\n  to Python when unstated.\r\n\r\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\r\n\r\n- [X] Yes\r\n\r\nGenerated-by: Google Gemini following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/72474/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.gi